---
/**
 * Python Runner tool page.
 */
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import PyRunner from '../../components/tools/PyRunner';
---

<ToolLayout slug="python-runner">
  <PyRunner client:load />

  <Fragment slot="about">
    <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">01 · Pyodide WebAssembly</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Full CPython runtime compiled to WebAssembly running directly in your browser tab.
          Standard library and <code>micropip</code> wheel installation supported.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Zero Backend: No external compute servers, accounts, or queues.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">02 · Web Worker Isolation</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Code executes inside an isolated background Web Worker thread. Infinite loops (<code
            >while True: pass</code
          >) can be safely terminated without locking the UI.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Safety: Automatic 60-second timeout ceiling + instant Stop interrupt.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hud-card p-5">
        <h3 class="eyebrow text-accent mb-2">03 · Package Registry</h3>
        <p class="text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Preconfigured environments load standard packages (NumPy, SciPy, pandas) and custom
          project wheels dynamically from PyPI.
        </p>
        <div class="text-faint mt-3 font-mono text-[11px]">
          Live Artifacts: Real execution pipelines in a single click.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hud-card border-warn mt-6 border-l-2 p-5">
      <h3 class="eyebrow text-warn mb-3">Operational Limits & Assumptions</h3>
      <ul class="text-muted grid gap-3 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:grid-cols-2">
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>No Raw TCP Sockets:</strong> In-browser Python cannot open raw OS sockets; <code
              >requests</code
            > and raw HTTP libraries fail without wasm shims.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>C/Rust Extensions:</strong> Native binary modules require precompiled WebAssembly
            wheels published by maintainers.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Execution Overhead:</strong> Wasm execution is ~2x to 5x slower than native host
            Python. Useful for verification, not micro-benchmarks.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span class="text-accent font-mono font-bold">·</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Worker Reset:</strong> Pressing Stop terminates the worker instance, clearing in-memory
            variables for a fresh restart.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
